 @steffenhoover905  No. They revealed 3 cards, all more powerful and more expensive. The 6800, costs $579 USD and allegedly performs about anywhere between 1% to 15% better then the 2080ti across the board, which will likely mean it'll outperform the base 3070. A 3070 ti/Super will likely be on par and/or outperform it.

The second was the 6800 XT, which trades blows with the 3080 for $50 USD less at $649 USD and takes up 320 watts. Lastly is the 3900 XT which comes in at $999 USD, takes up 320 watts, and trades blows with the 3090. Both the 6800 and 6800 XT release November 18, while the 3900 XT releases December 8.

The RDNA2 GPU's are pretty impressive cards, a substantial jump over the RDNA1 cards, but none of the revealed cards are coming in at $500 USD or less. I'm sure we'll see the 3700 series and the 3600 series in the not too distant future to get their usual mass market consumers, but I wouldn't expect a release or even a reveal for them this year.

