 @ace_971  sigh bandwidth is how quickly you can move information to and from the memory, which is great and works fantastically, not got an issue there, what you are overlooking is that the cpu and gpu have to talk more (usually via a memory controller) so that they dont use the same space.
This wont use any bandwidth because its not moving information into free/allocated memory, but it will slow down allocation of that memory as its having to tell the cpu and gpu what they can and cannot use, and trust me, it slows it down, no matter how large a bandwidth is.
This is why dedicated memory is faster, you don't have the same amount of instructions going back and forth between several different components.

